{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And Leah said, 'bagad.'</b> An expression of betrayal: even though I gave him my handmaid, he should not have lain with her, since I have borne him four sons. And even though he came to Rachel's handmaid — Rachel had no sons. But the second son that her handmaid bore she named Asher, which means, it is praise for me that I let him lie with my handmaid." "<b>Bagad</b> is written; <i>ba gad</i> is read. Another interpretation: two words — <i>ba gadud</i>, a troop and host of sons that I have already borne four, and now my handmaid one."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:06:43.278128488Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}